1
00:00:05,834 --> 00:00:07,358
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,383 --> 00:00:09,008
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:10,627 --> 00:00:12,461
(Episode 14)

4
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:15,537
What kind of life have you had?

5
00:00:25,252 --> 00:00:29,981
What kind of life have you been living,
these past eight years since you left me?

6
00:00:36,294 --> 00:00:37,421
Gyu Rim.

7
00:00:40,012 --> 00:00:43,593
You'll wake Gyeol. Please close the door.

8
00:01:57,823 --> 00:01:59,132
What happened?

9
00:01:59,419 --> 00:02:03,294
How badly did they beat him
that he needs surgery? Poor Seong Uk.

10
00:02:03,941 --> 00:02:08,191
He lost some teeth, and the surgery
is for cartilage he broke in the fall...

11
00:02:08,216 --> 00:02:11,133
Who was it? Who did this to my son...

12
00:02:12,211 --> 00:02:13,919
Did he run into gangsters?

13
00:02:15,002 --> 00:02:18,711
No gangsters. One guy,
I mean, one man beat him up...

14
00:02:19,294 --> 00:02:23,877
I don't know him. He says he's
an old friend of Seong Uk's.

15
00:02:24,461 --> 00:02:27,169
- What?
- Mercy.

16
00:02:28,252 --> 00:02:30,461
Mercy on us.

17
00:02:30,461 --> 00:02:32,169
Get up.

18
00:02:33,747 --> 00:02:37,210
Our wedding is only a week away.
What do we do?

19
00:02:42,332 --> 00:02:45,874
I did some boxing when I was young...

20
00:02:46,877 --> 00:02:50,193
Usually it was one punch, three teeth,

21
00:02:51,544 --> 00:02:54,188
but he really lost six of them?

22
00:02:55,252 --> 00:03:00,127
If your fist is that strong,
you should have held back even more.

23
00:03:00,377 --> 00:03:04,836
How could you beat up a man that badly
and call him a close friend?

24
00:03:05,836 --> 00:03:09,669
I didn't beat up a man.
I beat up an animal.

25
00:03:10,627 --> 00:03:11,627
Sorry?

26
00:03:26,044 --> 00:03:30,320
You're up? How long have you been there?

27
00:03:32,419 --> 00:03:34,065
It's fine. It's nothing.

28
00:03:34,752 --> 00:03:37,919
Doesn't everybody have some secret
about how they were born?

29
00:03:42,961 --> 00:03:45,183
My dad is only 160 centimeters tall.

30
00:03:45,377 --> 00:03:49,127
I've just never asked,
but he might not be my real dad.

31
00:03:52,627 --> 00:03:54,502
Did you meet the Chairman?

32
00:03:56,377 --> 00:04:00,536
Did he say, "I am your father?"
Are you supposed to call him Dad now?

33
00:04:01,651 --> 00:04:05,336
Hold on, now that I think about it,

34
00:04:05,461 --> 00:04:09,252
is your family cursed with birth secrets?
Little Han Gyeol too.

35
00:04:10,086 --> 00:04:14,544
You just let it go, but for all we know,
he could be your son.

36
00:04:14,725 --> 00:04:16,126
Keep it down, would you?

37
00:04:18,211 --> 00:04:22,442
I thought birth secrets only happened
on TV. They're everywhere.

38
00:04:22,467 --> 00:04:24,508
I said keep it down, you idiot.

39
00:04:25,336 --> 00:04:27,033
"Keep it down, you idiot."

40
00:04:56,086 --> 00:04:58,461
If there's anything I can do to help...

41
00:05:03,211 --> 00:05:04,627
Help?

42
00:05:06,711 --> 00:05:08,794
What could you possibly do, Kim Mu Jin?

43
00:05:35,586 --> 00:05:37,544
You could just tell me the truth.

44
00:05:39,044 --> 00:05:41,211
Tell you what truth?

45
00:05:41,711 --> 00:05:43,314
I really don't know.

46
00:05:44,086 --> 00:05:47,029
I came back from a business trip
and there you were.

47
00:05:47,461 --> 00:05:51,627
They said it was your 100-day party,
and I even ate the rice cake.

48
00:05:52,336 --> 00:05:56,602
Your daughter had a baby.
Where were you, Grandpa?

49
00:05:56,763 --> 00:05:58,706
Out earning a living.

50
00:05:58,969 --> 00:06:04,104
And did your mother ask me
before she went and had you?

51
00:06:04,961 --> 00:06:08,794
I have plenty to be mad about,
and none of it was deserved.

52
00:06:09,419 --> 00:06:13,961
At my age, with these looks,
you've got people calling me Grandpa.

53
00:06:16,545 --> 00:06:18,387
You don't like me, do you?

54
00:06:20,461 --> 00:06:23,282
I didn't at first. Come on, belly...

55
00:06:24,919 --> 00:06:28,377
But what could I do? You've got
my blood in you. You're family.

56
00:06:29,502 --> 00:06:33,711
If I didn't have your blood in me,
you wouldn't like me, would you?

57
00:06:33,919 --> 00:06:36,419
What are you talking about at this hour?

58
00:06:37,044 --> 00:06:38,336
Out. Get out, now.

59
00:06:38,586 --> 00:06:40,794
You're the reason I can't push, kid.

60
00:06:41,502 --> 00:06:43,836
I'm not your grandson.

61
00:06:44,044 --> 00:06:45,586
Stress.

62
00:06:45,752 --> 00:06:47,836
Hey, go back to sleep.

63
00:06:47,961 --> 00:06:52,127
You're talking in your sleep.
Go on, get some rest. Go.

64
00:06:54,211 --> 00:06:56,357
Gyeol, are you in the bathroom?

65
00:06:57,044 --> 00:06:59,789
Hey, Gyu Rim. Get Gyeol out of here, now.

66
00:07:00,211 --> 00:07:03,252
What kind of kid talks in his sleep
like he's wide awake?

67
00:07:03,752 --> 00:07:05,461
Get out so I can push. Hurry.

68
00:07:13,066 --> 00:07:18,292
Gyeol, your grandpa's using the bathroom.
What were you doing in there?

69
00:07:19,544 --> 00:07:22,443
Asking him who I am.

70
00:07:23,711 --> 00:07:27,897
Who else would you be?
His grandson and my son.

71
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:31,169
Gyeol.

72
00:07:32,627 --> 00:07:34,436
Don't worry about me.

73
00:07:38,502 --> 00:07:40,584
That's no way to talk to me.

74
00:07:44,336 --> 00:07:46,411
And why do you keep speaking so formally?

75
00:07:47,336 --> 00:07:50,987
Why the sudden formality with me,
like you're somebody else's kid?

76
00:07:51,079 --> 00:07:52,370
Because I am somebody else's kid.

77
00:07:52,577 --> 00:07:53,836
Gyeol.

78
00:07:54,461 --> 00:07:58,568
And because you're not my mother, ma'am.

79
00:08:11,365 --> 00:08:13,102
What is he talking about?

80
00:08:16,544 --> 00:08:19,247
Uncles. I need to talk to you.

81
00:08:20,247 --> 00:08:23,186
Gyu O, hurry.

82
00:08:28,309 --> 00:08:29,816
What time is it?

83
00:08:36,397 --> 00:08:37,848
A little after five.

84
00:08:40,294 --> 00:08:42,209
What's going on at this hour?

85
00:08:42,643 --> 00:08:45,856
Sorry, but it's really important to me.

86
00:08:48,002 --> 00:08:49,385
Important? What is it?

87
00:08:49,502 --> 00:08:52,412
There's a secret about how I was born.

88
00:08:53,114 --> 00:08:54,114
What?

89
00:08:54,794 --> 00:08:56,002
My mother...

90
00:08:57,877 --> 00:09:00,071
I'm not Han Gyu Rim's son.

91
00:09:00,544 --> 00:09:04,455
What are you talking about?
If not a son, then a daughter?

92
00:09:05,419 --> 00:09:08,709
Did you see my mother give birth to me?

93
00:09:10,427 --> 00:09:13,147
No, I was in the army.

94
00:09:14,252 --> 00:09:17,481
When I got leave, you were already
the size of a caterpillar.

95
00:09:19,627 --> 00:09:22,258
So you didn't see me being born, right?

96
00:09:24,377 --> 00:09:28,047
What are you talking about at this hour?

97
00:09:28,711 --> 00:09:29,794
Did you fight with your mom?

98
00:09:37,711 --> 00:09:39,752
Gyu Seo!

99
00:09:40,586 --> 00:09:41,627
What?

100
00:09:41,752 --> 00:09:44,444
Did you see my mother give birth to me?

101
00:09:44,711 --> 00:09:46,731
Did you see her give birth to me?

102
00:09:48,044 --> 00:09:50,144
No, I didn't.

103
00:10:01,169 --> 00:10:05,461
See? Not one person.

104
00:10:08,503 --> 00:10:14,068
Nobody saw me being born.

105
00:10:34,211 --> 00:10:35,502
Why are you sitting there like that?

106
00:10:37,586 --> 00:10:40,752
Gyeol, let's talk.

107
00:10:43,544 --> 00:10:44,586
That little brat.

108
00:10:45,877 --> 00:10:47,252
Morning, Gyeol.

109
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:54,277
Gyu Rim, what's with Gyeol?

110
00:10:56,901 --> 00:11:00,505
You really didn't give birth to him?

111
00:11:04,294 --> 00:11:05,696
He's my son.

112
00:11:06,252 --> 00:11:10,294
I'm not asking if he's your son.
I'm asking if you gave birth to him.

113
00:11:10,336 --> 00:11:13,544
Yes, I gave birth to him.

114
00:11:14,669 --> 00:11:16,135
He's my son.

115
00:11:16,419 --> 00:11:17,711
Right. Of course.

116
00:11:17,794 --> 00:11:22,044
Why would you raise a kid
you didn't give birth to?

117
00:11:22,169 --> 00:11:24,252
With everyone pointing at you
and calling you a single mom...

118
00:11:24,919 --> 00:11:25,961
Honestly...

119
00:11:26,169 --> 00:11:27,877
Where did Gyeol hear something like that?

120
00:11:28,794 --> 00:11:32,669
It's the kids teasing him
about being found under a bridge.

121
00:11:33,252 --> 00:11:36,336
Just show him an ultrasound
from when you were pregnant.

122
00:11:36,408 --> 00:11:37,949
That'll settle it.

123
00:11:45,086 --> 00:11:50,021
Hey, is Gyeol actually her son? For real?

124
00:11:51,836 --> 00:11:54,629
Are you actually my dad? For real?

125
00:11:55,919 --> 00:11:57,904
Please tell me you aren't.

126
00:11:59,961 --> 00:12:01,304
I'm washing my hands.

127
00:12:05,627 --> 00:12:10,171
Gyeol, you don't want to talk to me?

128
00:12:10,711 --> 00:12:12,502
No. I don't, ma'am.

129
00:12:48,586 --> 00:12:50,419
Seo Hyeon's father told you, didn't he?

130
00:12:52,608 --> 00:12:54,316
That Gyu Rim is my daughter.

131
00:12:55,816 --> 00:12:56,959
That's why...

132
00:12:59,002 --> 00:13:01,961
I fought you and Seo Hyeon so hard.

133
00:13:04,642 --> 00:13:05,642
Yes.

134
00:13:08,502 --> 00:13:09,836
I'm sorry, Mu Jin.

135
00:13:12,627 --> 00:13:17,502
To you, to Seo Hyeon's father,
to Seo Hyeon...

136
00:13:19,502 --> 00:13:21,877
I've done something unforgivable.

137
00:13:24,877 --> 00:13:29,127
How can the world be this small?

138
00:13:30,586 --> 00:13:33,586
How can it possibly be this...

139
00:13:34,377 --> 00:13:38,877
Don't you owe Gyu Rim an apology?

140
00:13:43,294 --> 00:13:47,669
I heard you never once saw her
after the divorce.

141
00:13:51,019 --> 00:13:54,774
Never called her, never went to find her.

142
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:58,502
You're still her mother...

143
00:13:59,877 --> 00:14:01,794
How your daughter was living,

144
00:14:02,002 --> 00:14:04,877
what kind of person she was becoming,
weren't you even curious?

145
00:14:05,794 --> 00:14:07,502
I was, but I held it in.

146
00:14:09,955 --> 00:14:11,746
I wanted to see her, but I held out.

147
00:14:14,211 --> 00:14:17,073
I forced myself to forget and moved on.

148
00:14:19,711 --> 00:14:21,165
So that I could survive.

149
00:14:23,297 --> 00:14:25,177
It felt like the only way to keep going...

150
00:14:31,075 --> 00:14:33,574
I wanted to be true to my new family.

151
00:14:34,947 --> 00:14:37,238
Seo Hyeon's father only has eyes for me,

152
00:14:38,227 --> 00:14:43,939
and Seo Hyeon clings to me
even knowing I'm not her real mother.

153
00:14:44,823 --> 00:14:51,046
I wanted to give something back
to them both.

154
00:14:51,817 --> 00:14:53,153
And Gyu Rim?

155
00:14:54,533 --> 00:14:56,693
She needed a mother too.

156
00:14:57,850 --> 00:15:02,567
She must have missed having a mom
every single day.

157
00:15:04,752 --> 00:15:06,509
Gyu Rim is a strong girl.

158
00:15:08,211 --> 00:15:10,398
Tough and steady.

159
00:15:12,252 --> 00:15:15,540
She would have gotten through it, and...

160
00:15:18,189 --> 00:15:20,502
held on. I believe in her.

161
00:15:20,795 --> 00:15:23,797
That's no excuse. She was a child too.

162
00:15:24,794 --> 00:15:27,211
A child who desperately needed a mother.

163
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:34,210
Apologize to her. Even if it's late.

164
00:15:37,347 --> 00:15:40,324
I won't see her. No, I can't.

165
00:15:40,407 --> 00:15:43,219
- Ma'am.
- I'll never see her as long as I live.

166
00:15:47,877 --> 00:15:49,379
Either way, for Gyu Rim,

167
00:15:52,894 --> 00:15:54,932
she's better off without a mother like me.

168
00:16:02,919 --> 00:16:07,694
You're cruel to the end,
and selfish to the end.

169
00:16:12,624 --> 00:16:16,022
You're right.

170
00:16:18,809 --> 00:16:22,396
I didn't know I could be this selfish
and this cruel either.

171
00:17:03,483 --> 00:17:04,586
Ma'am.

172
00:17:08,002 --> 00:17:09,318
Why are you following me?

173
00:17:10,365 --> 00:17:12,740
In case you skip school and wander off.

174
00:17:13,086 --> 00:17:16,449
No matter how hard things get,
I don't cut class.

175
00:17:16,711 --> 00:17:20,919
I know. I know, but just in case.

176
00:17:21,002 --> 00:17:22,002
Ma'am.

177
00:17:22,044 --> 00:17:23,794
Could you please stop calling me that?

178
00:17:24,377 --> 00:17:26,259
Since when am I your ma'am?

179
00:17:26,377 --> 00:17:27,752
Then what, big sister?

180
00:17:28,044 --> 00:17:30,669
My friends already think it's strange...

181
00:17:30,725 --> 00:17:32,850
that my mom is so young, like an idol.

182
00:17:35,052 --> 00:17:36,934
I'm your mother, Gyeol.

183
00:17:37,752 --> 00:17:41,211
I can shout that I'm your mother
loud enough for the world to hear.

184
00:17:41,336 --> 00:17:42,377
Forget it.

185
00:17:42,544 --> 00:17:43,711
I mean it.

186
00:17:44,794 --> 00:17:47,586
I'll shout it until you believe me.

187
00:17:47,627 --> 00:17:50,752
Ma'am, you're a total introvert.

188
00:17:51,127 --> 00:17:53,787
You hate being embarrassed
more than anything.

189
00:17:57,294 --> 00:17:59,211
I'm Gyeol's mother!

190
00:17:59,669 --> 00:18:02,147
I'm Han Gyeol's mother!

191
00:18:02,669 --> 00:18:07,153
- I'm Han Gyu Rim, Han Gyeol's mother!
- Stop it. I said stop.

192
00:18:07,178 --> 00:18:11,211
Han Gyeol is my son, and I wouldn't trade
him for all of Korea!

193
00:18:11,251 --> 00:18:12,477
- Hello.
- Stop it.

194
00:18:12,502 --> 00:18:14,086
- Hi, get inside.
- Han Gyeol is my son!

195
00:18:14,294 --> 00:18:15,544
- Han Gyeol is!
- Stop it.

196
00:18:15,544 --> 00:18:19,211
The son Han Gyu Rim loves most
in this whole world!

197
00:18:19,236 --> 00:18:21,311
Mom, stop. Please stop.

198
00:18:22,461 --> 00:18:24,002
Will you believe me now?

199
00:18:25,519 --> 00:18:26,602
Han Gyeol.

200
00:18:30,586 --> 00:18:32,752
Your mom is amazing, Han Gyeol.

201
00:18:32,777 --> 00:18:36,693
I wish I had a mom as cool
and pretty as yours.

202
00:18:37,098 --> 00:18:38,586
Hello, Ms. Kwon.

203
00:18:40,877 --> 00:18:42,544
I'll head in first.

204
00:18:44,461 --> 00:18:49,044
Gyeol, listen to your teacher
and be good to your friends.

205
00:18:49,919 --> 00:18:52,961
I'll take good care of him,
so please don't worry.

206
00:18:53,243 --> 00:18:54,243
Thank you.

207
00:18:56,794 --> 00:18:59,511
Han Gyeol, wait up.

208
00:19:06,970 --> 00:19:08,292
Han Gyeol.

209
00:19:14,895 --> 00:19:17,104
I'm exhausted.

210
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:25,497
This is driving me up the wall.

211
00:19:25,669 --> 00:19:27,419
Why won't you settle? Why?

212
00:19:27,711 --> 00:19:29,461
Your mom's got plenty of money.

213
00:19:29,669 --> 00:19:32,836
I did nothing wrong. Why would I settle?

214
00:19:33,002 --> 00:19:35,002
I'm never settling.

215
00:19:36,086 --> 00:19:38,211
Just go.

216
00:19:38,711 --> 00:19:40,269
Are you getting back at me right now?

217
00:19:40,294 --> 00:19:43,919
Dumping everything you've held in
all this time to get revenge?

218
00:19:44,002 --> 00:19:46,752
I settle scores. I don't get revenge.

219
00:19:48,502 --> 00:19:51,252
If I'd known Seong Uk
was that kind of scum,

220
00:19:51,252 --> 00:19:53,836
I'd have destroyed him
before you ever met him.

221
00:19:54,044 --> 00:19:56,544
Honestly, this is all Han Gyu Rim's fault.

222
00:19:56,919 --> 00:19:59,461
If not for her, I'd have
never crossed paths with someone like you.

223
00:20:00,127 --> 00:20:02,711
She's never been any help. Not once.

224
00:20:02,736 --> 00:20:04,944
Blame the right person.

225
00:20:05,282 --> 00:20:10,309
If not for your sister, would you
even be standing upright right now?

226
00:20:10,544 --> 00:20:14,377
Forget it. You've completely wrecked
my wedding.

227
00:20:14,586 --> 00:20:17,502
Seong Uk can't have a ceremony
or a honeymoon in that condition.

228
00:20:17,669 --> 00:20:19,111
How are you going to pay for that?

229
00:20:19,377 --> 00:20:23,002
They say the penalties are astronomical.
How will you pay for them?

230
00:20:23,044 --> 00:20:27,002
I'll sell my body if I have to,
so don't worry about the fees.

231
00:20:27,803 --> 00:20:32,907
But I'm never settling over
hitting Seong Uk.

232
00:20:32,932 --> 00:20:34,140
Heung Sik.

233
00:20:35,552 --> 00:20:38,491
They say birds of a feather
flock together...

234
00:20:38,589 --> 00:20:42,727
Somehow you two found each other
like a matched set.

235
00:20:45,777 --> 00:20:50,069
Consider me your guardian
and call this wedding off.

236
00:20:50,711 --> 00:20:52,552
This is my final warning.

237
00:20:52,577 --> 00:20:54,785
Guardian, my foot.

238
00:20:55,231 --> 00:20:58,780
Fine, don't settle. Just try settling.

239
00:20:58,816 --> 00:21:02,051
Don't settle, and go rot in prison,
Cho Heung Sik.

240
00:21:02,076 --> 00:21:03,451
What do I do?

241
00:21:03,516 --> 00:21:07,972
Enough of this. Which lockup
did you say my Heung Sik is in?

242
00:21:08,294 --> 00:21:10,586
Instead of going to the lockup,
settle first.

243
00:21:10,836 --> 00:21:13,336
You have to settle
to get Cho Heung Sik out.

244
00:21:13,361 --> 00:21:16,519
Right. Settle.

245
00:21:16,544 --> 00:21:18,461
Where do I go and how do I settle?

246
00:21:18,652 --> 00:21:20,152
You settle with me.

247
00:21:20,461 --> 00:21:22,502
Twenty weeks of recovery, six teeth gone,

248
00:21:22,544 --> 00:21:25,586
surgery, treatment, hospital stay,
nursing care, emotional damages,

249
00:21:25,711 --> 00:21:29,803
and the penalties on the wedding,
reception, and honeymoon.

250
00:21:30,722 --> 00:21:32,199
And how much is that?

251
00:21:33,002 --> 00:21:35,979
I heard you own three more shops
besides this one.

252
00:21:36,682 --> 00:21:37,977
Sell just one.

253
00:21:39,332 --> 00:21:40,592
The nerve.

254
00:21:40,877 --> 00:21:44,752
What kind of nonsense is this sly girl
spouting off?

255
00:21:44,878 --> 00:21:47,906
So you'll leave Cho Heung Sik
rotting in a cell?

256
00:21:48,419 --> 00:21:51,034
You'll let your son get a criminal record?

257
00:21:56,877 --> 00:21:58,669
It's crushing you, isn't it?

258
00:21:58,877 --> 00:22:01,086
I feel like I'm losing my mind too.

259
00:22:01,377 --> 00:22:03,169
So before word spreads any further...

260
00:22:03,211 --> 00:22:06,586
Gyeol's mother was born in March,
Year of the Dog,

261
00:22:06,961 --> 00:22:11,794
and her sister came 11 months later, so...

262
00:22:13,961 --> 00:22:16,213
So you were born in February,
Year of the Pig?

263
00:22:16,794 --> 00:22:18,544
Why do you need my birthday?

264
00:22:19,127 --> 00:22:21,251
The fortune teller's good.

265
00:22:21,544 --> 00:22:27,002
The Wolseondang fortune teller told me
to watch out for a February Pig...

266
00:22:27,211 --> 00:22:31,294
That I shouldn't go near one
for all the rice cake in the world...

267
00:22:31,794 --> 00:22:32,919
What is she talking about?

268
00:22:33,044 --> 00:22:37,252
She said if my Heung Sik
gets close to a February Pig,

269
00:22:37,419 --> 00:22:40,169
everything would go up in flames...

270
00:22:40,252 --> 00:22:42,627
- Su Nam.
- Go! Are you going or not?

271
00:22:42,836 --> 00:22:46,794
Forget settling. I won't trade a word
with a February Pig,

272
00:22:46,961 --> 00:22:48,086
so get lost!

273
00:22:49,336 --> 00:22:52,294
Just try hovering around my Heung Sik.

274
00:22:52,627 --> 00:22:57,127
Then you and I
will be settling over attempted murder.

275
00:22:57,502 --> 00:23:00,211
What's all this February Pig nonsense?

276
00:23:00,544 --> 00:23:03,461
Su Nam, don't you lose your mind too.

277
00:23:03,627 --> 00:23:05,419
Are you really going
to give your son a record?

278
00:23:05,502 --> 00:23:07,044
Go! Are you going or not?

279
00:23:07,461 --> 00:23:11,963
Do I have to throw spinach water
in your face to make you leave?

280
00:23:13,704 --> 00:23:15,869
There's no reasoning with you.

281
00:23:19,407 --> 00:23:21,409
February Pigs really scare you,
don't they?

282
00:23:21,546 --> 00:23:26,044
If this wedding falls apart,
I'll just go marry Cho Heung Sik.

283
00:23:27,711 --> 00:23:30,718
No! The nerve of her.

284
00:24:12,670 --> 00:24:16,433
Hey, can't you see me?

285
00:24:19,371 --> 00:24:20,531
What are you doing here?

286
00:24:21,037 --> 00:24:23,136
- You didn't go to work?
- Cho Heung Sik, that...

287
00:24:28,817 --> 00:24:30,337
I didn't come home last night.

288
00:24:31,431 --> 00:24:33,017
You didn't even notice, did you?

289
00:24:35,436 --> 00:24:36,757
You're not a child,

290
00:24:37,211 --> 00:24:39,210
so do I have to worry about you too now?

291
00:24:39,570 --> 00:24:41,329
Cutting ties is fine with me,

292
00:24:41,601 --> 00:24:43,144
but I'm not married yet.

293
00:24:43,531 --> 00:24:45,943
Let's cut ties after the wedding,
so it means something.

294
00:24:47,724 --> 00:24:48,724
I'm off.

295
00:25:01,651 --> 00:25:03,044
There's something I've been wondering.

296
00:25:03,637 --> 00:25:07,609
A type O mother having a type AB child,

297
00:25:07,997 --> 00:25:09,777
is that really so impossible?

298
00:25:13,170 --> 00:25:17,301
- What?
- Isn't it possible if the father is AB?

299
00:25:18,251 --> 00:25:20,874
Are you asking me to show
just how ignorant you are?

300
00:25:24,176 --> 00:25:25,937
Why am I such an idiot?

301
00:25:26,471 --> 00:25:28,651
How did I not see it, honestly?

302
00:25:30,585 --> 00:25:32,083
Gyeol isn't your son, is he?

303
00:25:33,437 --> 00:25:35,124
He called and asked me...

304
00:25:35,477 --> 00:25:36,870
whether I knew who his real mother is.

305
00:25:37,550 --> 00:25:40,458
- And what did you say?
- That I didn't know.

306
00:25:40,584 --> 00:25:42,824
That I came back from studying abroad
and there he was.

307
00:25:42,826 --> 00:25:44,571
Why would you say that?

308
00:25:45,130 --> 00:25:47,271
You could have just said I'm his mother.

309
00:25:47,351 --> 00:25:48,858
I only state facts.

310
00:25:52,803 --> 00:25:54,743
So Gyeol really isn't your son?

311
00:25:55,030 --> 00:25:57,247
Why on earth would you raise a kid
who isn't even yours?

312
00:25:57,993 --> 00:26:01,117
Enough. Let's drop it.

313
00:26:03,636 --> 00:26:06,729
Hey, who are Gyeol's real parents?

314
00:26:06,731 --> 00:26:09,252
- What do they do?
- You never changed one diaper.

315
00:26:09,346 --> 00:26:10,657
Keep your mouth shut.

316
00:26:11,317 --> 00:26:12,884
Gyeol is my son.

317
00:26:12,924 --> 00:26:15,770
You've lost it. You've completely lost it.

318
00:26:16,231 --> 00:26:18,204
Is charity your talent
and sacrifice your hobby?

319
00:26:18,504 --> 00:26:20,074
Not even married, called a single mom,

320
00:26:20,076 --> 00:26:21,689
with the whole world pointing at you!

321
00:26:21,691 --> 00:26:23,464
You don't care about me.

322
00:26:24,064 --> 00:26:25,735
Be consistent and keep pretending.

323
00:26:25,969 --> 00:26:27,150
You're the worst.

324
00:26:28,397 --> 00:26:30,110
The twins weren't enough for you?

325
00:26:30,664 --> 00:26:33,257
Why do you go out of your way
to sacrifice for everyone?

326
00:26:33,497 --> 00:26:36,890
Just take government money
and open an orphanage already!

327
00:26:38,177 --> 00:26:39,930
Why wait for the wedding?

328
00:26:40,370 --> 00:26:42,643
Let's cut ties right this second.

329
00:26:44,881 --> 00:26:47,457
Is my nose broken? The back of my head,
the front of my head.

330
00:26:48,130 --> 00:26:50,317
Did you all team up today
to finish me off?

331
00:26:50,726 --> 00:26:52,590
Hey, Han Gyu Rim!

332
00:27:08,323 --> 00:27:09,464
Have you eaten?

333
00:27:10,890 --> 00:27:12,437
I moved out of the house.

334
00:27:22,537 --> 00:27:24,503
I'll ask you one last time.

335
00:27:28,491 --> 00:27:30,017
You were playing a joke on me, right?

336
00:27:31,977 --> 00:27:35,072
You always loved messing with me, Dad.

337
00:27:36,337 --> 00:27:38,127
You were joking this time too, right?

338
00:27:48,291 --> 00:27:52,077
You really got me.
I fell for it completely.

339
00:27:52,830 --> 00:27:54,317
Just say unfreeze already.

340
00:27:54,683 --> 00:27:57,990
Say the game's over,
that I can stop being frozen.

341
00:28:00,684 --> 00:28:02,468
I said stop joking.

342
00:28:02,636 --> 00:28:05,577
This joke isn't funny.
I hate it more than anything.

343
00:28:06,568 --> 00:28:07,725
Listen,

344
00:28:08,486 --> 00:28:11,697
I'm going to step back
from running the company for a while.

345
00:28:12,237 --> 00:28:14,747
I don't know if it'll be one year or two,

346
00:28:15,409 --> 00:28:18,797
but I'll be resting at the Jeju farm
with your mother in the meantime.

347
00:28:20,224 --> 00:28:23,400
Until your heart settles
and you sort things out.

348
00:28:25,370 --> 00:28:26,703
So it's real, then?

349
00:28:30,116 --> 00:28:33,231
You stir up all this chaos
and then run away?

350
00:28:33,233 --> 00:28:34,233
Like a coward?

351
00:28:37,114 --> 00:28:39,031
My mother really has an iron stomach.

352
00:28:39,544 --> 00:28:41,716
How does she eat with someone
as awful as you,

353
00:28:41,741 --> 00:28:43,845
sleep beside you,

354
00:28:44,086 --> 00:28:46,557
talk to you, breathe the same air?

355
00:28:46,691 --> 00:28:48,684
My mother must not be human.

356
00:28:51,031 --> 00:28:52,637
Divorce her first.

357
00:28:55,001 --> 00:28:56,928
My mother is too soft-hearted
to say it herself,

358
00:28:56,959 --> 00:28:58,603
so I'm saying it for her.

359
00:28:59,691 --> 00:29:02,131
Divorce her and let her go.

360
00:29:03,771 --> 00:29:05,768
You're the one at fault here,

361
00:29:05,770 --> 00:29:08,030
so sign everything you own over to her.

362
00:29:09,603 --> 00:29:10,629
Seo Hyeon.

363
00:29:12,284 --> 00:29:13,524
That's what I came to say.

364
00:29:16,964 --> 00:29:18,487
Once you move out,

365
00:29:18,715 --> 00:29:20,583
I'll move back in and live with her.

366
00:29:35,226 --> 00:29:37,486
(Chairwoman Hong Ok Seon)

367
00:29:41,777 --> 00:29:42,883
Good.

368
00:29:44,364 --> 00:29:45,364
Very good.

369
00:29:47,277 --> 00:29:48,617
It's all good, but...

370
00:29:48,730 --> 00:29:51,769
what's the point of a fantastic product...

371
00:29:51,771 --> 00:29:55,230
if the marketing behind it
isn't just as fantastic?

372
00:29:56,864 --> 00:29:59,190
Still no word from the artist Joel?

373
00:30:00,204 --> 00:30:01,204
No.

374
00:30:01,951 --> 00:30:04,953
I went to the address listed
on the website myself,

375
00:30:05,268 --> 00:30:08,804
but he keeps his own hours,
so catching him isn't easy.

376
00:30:09,237 --> 00:30:11,955
I sent a message
on social media, no reply,

377
00:30:12,242 --> 00:30:16,843
and hardly any of the staff
have even seen his face.

378
00:30:17,345 --> 00:30:20,369
This will be a headache
even if the project lands.

379
00:30:20,371 --> 00:30:22,631
How do we work with someone
who does things his own way?

380
00:30:27,197 --> 00:30:30,675
- Yes?
- You have a visitor, ma'am.

381
00:30:30,891 --> 00:30:31,911
Who?

382
00:30:38,898 --> 00:30:41,318
I'll head out too.

383
00:30:48,204 --> 00:30:50,333
You met Seo Hyeon's father, didn't you?

384
00:30:52,224 --> 00:30:54,801
He spouted such absolute nonsense...

385
00:30:55,016 --> 00:30:58,244
that I told him to get psychiatric help
and come back.

386
00:31:01,404 --> 00:31:04,453
I'm sorry for putting you through that.

387
00:31:07,284 --> 00:31:10,330
Did some man who looks like my Mu Jin
run a con on you?

388
00:31:14,063 --> 00:31:17,232
If you don't approve of him,

389
00:31:17,234 --> 00:31:20,651
you could just say so honestly.

390
00:31:20,917 --> 00:31:24,317
Whose head did this idea even come out of?

391
00:31:25,117 --> 00:31:27,710
Shouldn't Jang Hun Tae be hospitalized?

392
00:31:29,291 --> 00:31:30,770
I'm sorry.

393
00:31:32,137 --> 00:31:36,174
I have nothing I can say in my defense.

394
00:31:36,276 --> 00:31:39,982
Where do you get off rejecting a catch
like my son?

395
00:31:41,500 --> 00:31:46,167
I gave you every courtesy I had
for Seo Hyeon's late mother's sake,

396
00:31:46,288 --> 00:31:47,564
and how dare you.

397
00:31:48,204 --> 00:31:49,550
You don't know your place.

398
00:31:51,074 --> 00:31:55,390
How could you turn down my son
in such a petty way?

399
00:31:57,784 --> 00:31:59,324
I'm sorry, ma'am.

400
00:32:00,951 --> 00:32:03,416
Why so meek all of a sudden?

401
00:32:03,927 --> 00:32:08,655
Look me in the eye and say it out loud.

402
00:32:08,754 --> 00:32:11,465
Say Mu Jin will never happen,
not over your dead body.

403
00:32:11,490 --> 00:32:13,544
Go on, drive me out of my mind.

404
00:32:16,965 --> 00:32:21,643
I'm done with Seo Hyeon too.

405
00:32:22,283 --> 00:32:24,216
Tell Hun Tae to delete my number,

406
00:32:24,247 --> 00:32:27,836
and that we're ending this long, ugly
connection right here.

407
00:32:29,356 --> 00:32:32,403
- Han Gyu Rim is my daughter.
- Who is?

408
00:32:34,444 --> 00:32:38,069
The girl Mu Jin used to see.

409
00:32:40,444 --> 00:32:42,750
The one you treated like a gold digger...

410
00:32:45,306 --> 00:32:46,424
That girl.

411
00:32:48,897 --> 00:32:52,910
She's the eldest daughter I left behind
when I divorced.

412
00:32:55,610 --> 00:32:58,783
What are you saying right now?

413
00:32:59,570 --> 00:33:02,525
That's why I fought Seo Hyeon
and Mu Jin...

414
00:33:02,643 --> 00:33:03,977
Not knowing my place.

415
00:33:06,831 --> 00:33:07,831
Hold on.

416
00:33:09,795 --> 00:33:11,240
Look here, Seo Hyeon's mother.

417
00:33:12,871 --> 00:33:14,157
Seo Hyeon's father...

418
00:33:16,137 --> 00:33:18,977
was afraid Seo Hyeon
would never look at me again,

419
00:33:20,051 --> 00:33:22,170
so he took the whole thing on himself.

420
00:33:22,919 --> 00:33:24,030
I can't believe this...

421
00:33:31,824 --> 00:33:33,477
- Have a seat over there.
- Yes.

422
00:33:48,917 --> 00:33:52,328
- One makgeolli, please.
- Coming up.

423
00:33:59,576 --> 00:34:00,705
Hello.

424
00:34:01,884 --> 00:34:04,696
- Do you know me?
- You don't know me?

425
00:34:08,217 --> 00:34:10,146
You're the grouper lady.

426
00:34:14,464 --> 00:34:15,662
Makgeolli.

427
00:34:17,356 --> 00:34:22,951
I kept telling myself you just looked
a lot like her.

428
00:34:23,456 --> 00:34:25,689
I've been to a wedding.

429
00:34:25,804 --> 00:34:29,865
You two know each other, so sit together.
There's no room anyway.

430
00:34:35,950 --> 00:34:37,144
Have a seat.

431
00:34:37,317 --> 00:34:38,877
- Sure.
- Sit down.

432
00:34:47,661 --> 00:34:50,964
Look, be honest with me.

433
00:34:52,048 --> 00:34:53,264
What is it you do?

434
00:34:54,510 --> 00:34:55,705
A sashimi place.

435
00:34:56,044 --> 00:34:57,864
You used to run one.

436
00:34:58,370 --> 00:35:00,264
I reopened it. Have to make a living.

437
00:35:01,503 --> 00:35:05,398
No way. Your whole vibe is different...

438
00:35:06,236 --> 00:35:09,862
You've got serious old-money energy...

439
00:35:10,939 --> 00:35:13,328
My sister runs a dry cleaner's,

440
00:35:13,330 --> 00:35:16,670
so I borrowed the nicest thing
she had in there.

441
00:35:21,411 --> 00:35:23,601
The wedding food must have been bad.

442
00:35:24,402 --> 00:35:25,577
Ordering makgeolli and all.

443
00:35:28,830 --> 00:35:31,157
Something happened
that left me speechless.

444
00:35:31,950 --> 00:35:34,374
You too? Same here.

445
00:35:35,310 --> 00:35:36,459
Want to bet?

446
00:35:37,267 --> 00:35:39,670
Whose story is more unbelievable.

447
00:35:41,217 --> 00:35:42,429
You're on.

448
00:35:45,571 --> 00:35:47,957
Never mind. I don't even want to say it.

449
00:35:48,877 --> 00:35:49,917
Go ahead.

450
00:35:50,798 --> 00:35:51,804
Fifty dollars on it.

451
00:36:11,517 --> 00:36:13,351
There's a woman my son used to see,

452
00:36:13,353 --> 00:36:15,360
and a woman he's seeing now,

453
00:36:15,362 --> 00:36:17,604
and the two of them have the same mother.

454
00:36:17,717 --> 00:36:19,563
I could not believe it...

455
00:36:20,757 --> 00:36:22,022
Could you say that one more time?

456
00:36:22,024 --> 00:36:23,391
I'm not following.

457
00:36:23,393 --> 00:36:25,545
Forget it. I hate repeating myself.

458
00:36:30,573 --> 00:36:33,788
The kid I raised thinking
he was my grandson,

459
00:36:34,703 --> 00:36:36,024
turns out he isn't.

460
00:36:42,944 --> 00:36:44,824
He's messaged me again.

461
00:36:45,377 --> 00:36:47,516
Asking me to tell him his birth secret.

462
00:36:47,541 --> 00:36:51,004
He's been calling, texting,
messaging nonstop...

463
00:36:52,345 --> 00:36:54,184
And I truly don't know.

464
00:37:04,817 --> 00:37:07,177
Keep the fifty.

465
00:37:30,684 --> 00:37:32,993
What are you staring at? Want a drink?

466
00:37:35,904 --> 00:37:36,920
It's not that.

467
00:37:38,241 --> 00:37:43,288
You look pretty impressive downing a shot,

468
00:37:43,839 --> 00:37:45,604
so I keep looking without meaning to.

469
00:37:46,311 --> 00:37:48,584
What? Are you hitting on me?

470
00:37:50,493 --> 00:37:53,037
No. Am I crazy?

471
00:37:54,137 --> 00:37:57,010
I am absolutely sick of women.

472
00:37:58,477 --> 00:38:01,307
Even if you really tried to seduce me,

473
00:38:02,356 --> 00:38:04,303
I would never fall for it.

474
00:38:07,157 --> 00:38:09,780
Not that I'd ever seduce you,

475
00:38:11,280 --> 00:38:12,884
but you'd fall for it.

476
00:38:15,091 --> 00:38:16,740
I said I wouldn't.

477
00:38:17,425 --> 00:38:19,089
When it comes to women,

478
00:38:20,396 --> 00:38:22,143
I have truly had enough.

479
00:38:26,645 --> 00:38:28,044
Have you only ever been lied to?

480
00:38:29,217 --> 00:38:30,324
Want to bet?

481
00:38:30,837 --> 00:38:32,890
Everything is a bet with you.

482
00:38:34,288 --> 00:38:38,506
Love betting too much and you go broke
overnight. Like me.

483
00:38:51,210 --> 00:38:52,210
Deal?

484
00:38:58,904 --> 00:38:59,904
Mu Jin.

485
00:39:01,824 --> 00:39:02,824
You're here.

486
00:39:04,964 --> 00:39:08,692
- Can I still call you that outside?
- Of course.

487
00:39:10,971 --> 00:39:11,971
What do you want to eat?

488
00:39:13,525 --> 00:39:16,190
In a bit. Have a seat first.

489
00:39:16,957 --> 00:39:17,957
Sure.

490
00:39:24,203 --> 00:39:27,971
Is it too much to ask about Gyu Rim,
how she's been since we broke up,

491
00:39:30,051 --> 00:39:31,944
right up to now?

492
00:39:33,583 --> 00:39:37,351
The last eight years.

493
00:39:38,644 --> 00:39:41,944
No. Why did it take you so long to ask?

494
00:39:43,331 --> 00:39:46,057
I've always been ready to answer.

495
00:39:48,230 --> 00:39:50,171
This is going to be a long story,

496
00:39:53,704 --> 00:39:57,382
so I'll get ice cream. Give me your card.

497
00:40:04,904 --> 00:40:07,997
Gyu Rim is a total wreck because of Gyeol.

498
00:40:08,717 --> 00:40:10,925
He says he has to know his birth secret,

499
00:40:11,093 --> 00:40:13,257
keeping the whole family up since dawn.

500
00:40:13,646 --> 00:40:17,650
Right. Gyeol came to me too.

501
00:40:20,931 --> 00:40:23,464
I'm not good at school, so I don't know.

502
00:40:23,689 --> 00:40:25,110
Is it certain...

503
00:40:25,376 --> 00:40:28,417
that a type O mother
can't have a type AB son? Really?

504
00:40:28,593 --> 00:40:31,143
No matter the father's blood type?

505
00:40:33,431 --> 00:40:36,259
I always thought Gyu Rim
gave birth to him...

506
00:40:38,190 --> 00:40:41,104
She even showed me a photo
of the baby in her belly.

507
00:40:41,220 --> 00:40:42,350
A photo?

508
00:40:46,070 --> 00:40:48,945
- She showed you an ultrasound?
- Yes.

509
00:40:49,311 --> 00:40:50,311
When?

510
00:40:51,676 --> 00:40:53,630
Eight years ago,
when I was in grade school.

511
00:40:54,037 --> 00:40:56,907
Looking back, it was an ultrasound,

512
00:40:57,361 --> 00:41:00,576
and she only showed me.
Said it was her baby.

513
00:41:01,542 --> 00:41:03,795
The baby even had a nickname.

514
00:41:04,116 --> 00:41:05,597
What was it...

515
00:41:09,492 --> 00:41:12,298
I remember. Hope.

516
00:41:14,906 --> 00:41:18,010
Her belly was out to here.

517
00:41:21,693 --> 00:41:27,110
That's why I thought
you might be Gyeol's father.

518
00:41:28,976 --> 00:41:30,497
What could have happened?

519
00:41:31,070 --> 00:41:33,869
She went to the hospital to have the baby,

520
00:41:35,205 --> 00:41:38,797
so could they have switched babies there?

521
00:42:00,633 --> 00:42:03,537
Start the car. Take me somewhere,
anywhere.

522
00:42:13,011 --> 00:42:14,556
Want to just run away?

523
00:42:16,163 --> 00:42:18,109
Cut off family, cut off everything,

524
00:42:18,111 --> 00:42:20,003
run away and live, just the two of us.

525
00:42:20,864 --> 00:42:24,248
Go somewhere with nobody around
and live, just us.

526
00:42:39,555 --> 00:42:42,830
How can you stop here
after I say run away?

527
00:42:47,883 --> 00:42:48,987
Have you eaten?

528
00:42:49,547 --> 00:42:53,663
Or should I get you a sandwich?

529
00:42:54,864 --> 00:42:57,064
Honestly, you were relieved, weren't you?

530
00:42:59,677 --> 00:43:01,926
You were dragged into this out of duty,

531
00:43:02,173 --> 00:43:04,663
and when they said it couldn't happen,
that it had to end,

532
00:43:05,171 --> 00:43:06,651
you were thrilled inside, weren't you?

533
00:43:10,383 --> 00:43:13,016
Strangely,
something never sat right with me.

534
00:43:13,655 --> 00:43:17,040
This feeling that we wouldn't make it...

535
00:43:17,608 --> 00:43:19,904
all the way. I don't know why.

536
00:43:23,751 --> 00:43:25,144
Let's get a meal sometime.

537
00:43:26,317 --> 00:43:29,519
Call me anytime you want something good.

538
00:43:31,097 --> 00:43:32,097
Sometime?

539
00:43:35,290 --> 00:43:37,009
You're only going to see me sometimes now?

540
00:43:38,729 --> 00:43:39,729
Yes.

541
00:43:42,516 --> 00:43:43,910
Let's only see each other sometimes now.

542
00:43:51,237 --> 00:43:54,669
It's not fair. It isn't right.

543
00:43:55,843 --> 00:43:58,303
I never got to do anything with you...

544
00:43:59,937 --> 00:44:03,051
Never went to a movie,
never took a trip...

545
00:44:04,038 --> 00:44:07,464
Never got couple rings,
never even kissed you...

546
00:44:09,124 --> 00:44:12,032
Where should I take you? I'll drive you.

547
00:44:13,736 --> 00:44:15,017
There's really no give, is there?

548
00:44:18,343 --> 00:44:20,443
You won't leave even a crack, will you?

549
00:44:28,963 --> 00:44:30,582
I'll go start the car.

550
00:44:37,704 --> 00:44:39,277
Don't see anyone.

551
00:44:39,957 --> 00:44:43,955
Don't love anyone. Live and die alone.

552
00:44:56,091 --> 00:44:57,897
Where will you go after you drop me off?

553
00:45:00,197 --> 00:45:01,197
To work.

554
00:45:07,016 --> 00:45:08,470
Go to Han Gyu Rim.

555
00:45:12,176 --> 00:45:14,840
I'm the one who held onto your leg
and kept you from going.

556
00:45:16,345 --> 00:45:17,604
Go to her.

557
00:45:20,711 --> 00:45:23,597
I don't know if I mean it
or I'm faking it,

558
00:45:24,838 --> 00:45:28,281
but it's a gift for doing your best by me.

559
00:45:30,484 --> 00:45:31,770
Go now, even now.

560
00:45:35,577 --> 00:45:37,261
And one favor.

561
00:45:38,315 --> 00:45:39,969
If the two of you get back together,

562
00:45:41,443 --> 00:45:43,197
hide from the world completely.

563
00:45:46,537 --> 00:45:49,297
Go somewhere I can never hear
a word about you,

564
00:45:50,024 --> 00:45:52,204
so I can't catch a single glimpse of you.

565
00:46:15,857 --> 00:46:17,470
Is it okay to be out here
with the shop open?

566
00:46:18,651 --> 00:46:22,463
Gyeol isn't coming out.

567
00:46:23,763 --> 00:46:27,389
All the other kids are out, but not him.

568
00:46:31,164 --> 00:46:32,404
Pull it together.

569
00:46:34,062 --> 00:46:36,875
I've never seen you this out of it.

570
00:46:37,730 --> 00:46:41,443
If you're like this,
Gyeol gets more confused and more anxious.

571
00:46:43,727 --> 00:46:47,324
All right. I'll pull it together.

572
00:46:49,037 --> 00:46:51,687
I'll wait for Gyeol, so get to the shop.

573
00:46:53,751 --> 00:46:55,551
You're not this irresponsible.

574
00:46:55,552 --> 00:46:57,445
This isn't like Han Gyu Rim at all.

575
00:47:02,050 --> 00:47:03,076
Gyu Rim.

576
00:47:06,476 --> 00:47:07,489
All right.

577
00:47:11,256 --> 00:47:13,584
- Take care of Gyeol.
- Sure.

578
00:47:24,444 --> 00:47:25,450
Gyu O.

579
00:47:28,526 --> 00:47:32,177
Gyeol is my son.

580
00:47:34,284 --> 00:47:35,297
I know.

581
00:47:35,817 --> 00:47:38,357
I wouldn't trade him for my own life.

582
00:47:39,663 --> 00:47:43,457
Gyu Rim. I know.

583
00:48:00,266 --> 00:48:03,487
Gyeol! Han Gyeol!

584
00:48:03,706 --> 00:48:06,671
First grade, class two, Han Gyeol!

585
00:48:07,051 --> 00:48:09,127
Gyeol. Han...

586
00:48:29,670 --> 00:48:30,750
Gyu O.

587
00:48:33,756 --> 00:48:36,629
- Gyeol.
- Why did you come to school?

588
00:48:38,537 --> 00:48:39,883
To pick you up.

589
00:48:40,051 --> 00:48:42,615
Why? In case I go off the rails?

590
00:48:43,931 --> 00:48:46,837
No, to buy you something good to eat.

591
00:48:47,110 --> 00:48:51,070
I'm fine. My teacher said she'd buy me
something good.

592
00:48:56,497 --> 00:48:58,877
- Let's go, Ms. Kwon.
- Sure.

593
00:49:14,617 --> 00:49:17,333
- Does it bother you?
- Sorry?

594
00:49:17,564 --> 00:49:22,088
We're eating pizza
while my uncle stands outside,

595
00:49:22,113 --> 00:49:23,428
does that bother you?

596
00:49:23,453 --> 00:49:24,990
No.

597
00:49:25,930 --> 00:49:27,505
It bothers me.

598
00:49:28,972 --> 00:49:32,657
But I still don't want
to talk to anyone in my family.

599
00:49:43,780 --> 00:49:48,768
Gyeol, I know you're thrown and shaken up,

600
00:49:48,793 --> 00:49:52,561
but avoiding your mom and family
like this isn't the answer.

601
00:49:53,376 --> 00:49:55,662
You're off school tomorrow anyway,

602
00:49:55,728 --> 00:49:57,670
so go somewhere nice with your mom,

603
00:49:57,672 --> 00:50:00,350
ask what you want to know
and let her explain.

604
00:50:02,064 --> 00:50:04,224
Your mom is the best there is.

605
00:50:04,350 --> 00:50:08,371
I've met Da Som's mom and Jae Beom's mom,
all of them,

606
00:50:08,478 --> 00:50:12,270
but I've never seen a mother
as devoted and loving as yours.

607
00:50:12,421 --> 00:50:13,847
I mean it.

608
00:50:14,097 --> 00:50:15,977
Ms. Kwon, I want to go.

609
00:50:16,002 --> 00:50:17,735
I don't want pizza.

610
00:50:17,810 --> 00:50:18,857
Gyeol.

611
00:50:22,804 --> 00:50:23,817
Han Gyeol.

612
00:50:24,217 --> 00:50:26,144
Ma'am, the bill?

613
00:50:30,377 --> 00:50:31,457
Han Gyeol.

614
00:50:33,604 --> 00:50:36,141
- Talk to me.
- I have nothing to say.

615
00:50:36,417 --> 00:50:37,877
I have something to say.

616
00:50:37,911 --> 00:50:40,557
I don't want to hear anything from you.

617
00:50:42,137 --> 00:50:43,811
You really have gone off the rails.

618
00:50:43,836 --> 00:50:45,578
You said you didn't know anything.

619
00:50:46,078 --> 00:50:48,130
You said you never saw her
give birth to me.

620
00:50:48,155 --> 00:50:50,959
I never saw my mom
give birth to me either.

621
00:50:52,464 --> 00:50:54,357
I need time to think.

622
00:50:54,470 --> 00:50:57,777
Please tell Ms. Han Gyu Rim that too.

623
00:51:00,023 --> 00:51:01,558
Ms. Han Gyu Rim?

624
00:51:01,732 --> 00:51:04,236
Do you know what state
your mother is in because of you?

625
00:51:04,470 --> 00:51:06,126
Watch your mouth.

626
00:51:06,151 --> 00:51:08,065
Calm down, Gyeol's uncle.

627
00:51:10,984 --> 00:51:12,772
Goodbye, Ms. Kwon.

628
00:51:15,823 --> 00:51:17,112
Hey, where are you going?

629
00:51:17,294 --> 00:51:19,010
That's the opposite way from home.

630
00:51:19,530 --> 00:51:21,290
I'm not going home.

631
00:51:21,451 --> 00:51:23,515
I'm going to Mu Jin's place.

632
00:51:24,344 --> 00:51:26,502
Why would you go there?

633
00:51:27,561 --> 00:51:29,944
Such a little thing giving me such grief.

634
00:51:29,969 --> 00:51:32,129
You can't act like a child yourself.

635
00:51:36,510 --> 00:51:39,799
Gyeol may be mature,
but he's still a child.

636
00:51:42,304 --> 00:51:44,670
If there's somewhere he wants to lean,

637
00:51:45,171 --> 00:51:47,104
let him lean there.

638
00:51:48,077 --> 00:51:49,690
As long as it's someone trustworthy.

639
00:51:57,323 --> 00:51:59,130
I never expected to meet you like this.

640
00:52:03,064 --> 00:52:06,030
Don't you know me? Han Gyu O.

641
00:52:06,216 --> 00:52:08,162
You really don't remember?

642
00:52:09,848 --> 00:52:13,243
No. I wiped it all clean.

643
00:52:15,476 --> 00:52:19,749
So please pretend not to know me either,

644
00:52:20,991 --> 00:52:22,857
if we happen to meet again.

645
00:52:37,956 --> 00:52:39,076
Gyu Rim.

646
00:52:42,803 --> 00:52:44,097
Where's Gyeol?

647
00:52:44,951 --> 00:52:48,083
I found him, but he went to Kim Mu Jin.

648
00:52:49,618 --> 00:52:52,397
Gyu Seo told me about him.

649
00:52:52,857 --> 00:52:55,998
Anyway, Gyeol's teacher says...

650
00:52:56,435 --> 00:53:00,410
if there's somewhere he wants to lean,
we should let him lean there.

651
00:53:03,976 --> 00:53:05,496
What is going on with Gyeol?

652
00:53:06,097 --> 00:53:08,010
Is he really not your son?

653
00:53:08,363 --> 00:53:09,883
Then why did you raise him?

654
00:53:10,751 --> 00:53:11,777
Go.

655
00:53:11,971 --> 00:53:15,727
Respecting your privacy,
everyone for themselves, that's all fine,

656
00:53:15,945 --> 00:53:17,650
but we're still family.

657
00:53:18,330 --> 00:53:22,170
Whose son Gyeol is, why you raised a boy
who isn't yours,

658
00:53:22,571 --> 00:53:24,443
can't you tell us that much?

659
00:53:27,744 --> 00:53:30,331
Gyeol is my son, Gyu O.

660
00:53:31,343 --> 00:53:35,040
Even if the sky falls, he's my son.

661
00:53:42,437 --> 00:53:43,523
Gyeol.

662
00:53:48,716 --> 00:53:50,110
Why are you sitting out here?

663
00:53:51,138 --> 00:53:53,751
Why did you leave me behind?

664
00:54:04,137 --> 00:54:07,817
Do you think I'm a baby?

665
00:54:08,551 --> 00:54:10,551
That doesn't mean I can give you coffee.

666
00:54:19,430 --> 00:54:21,956
You came straight here without going home?

667
00:54:21,981 --> 00:54:22,981
Yes.

668
00:54:24,050 --> 00:54:26,610
Did you tell your mom
you were coming here?

669
00:54:26,704 --> 00:54:28,677
Gyu O probably did.

670
00:54:29,190 --> 00:54:32,169
Did he? Good, then.

671
00:54:32,958 --> 00:54:34,871
I'm a bother to you, aren't I?

672
00:54:35,377 --> 00:54:38,510
No. Don't say things like that.

673
00:54:39,158 --> 00:54:40,864
But I can't help it.

674
00:54:41,036 --> 00:54:45,436
I have nowhere to go but here,

675
00:54:45,482 --> 00:54:47,648
until I find my real mother.

676
00:54:49,470 --> 00:54:53,236
Your mother said no matter what,
you're her real son.

677
00:54:54,251 --> 00:54:59,484
But nobody saw her give birth to me.

678
00:55:08,817 --> 00:55:11,304
- Mu Jin.
- Yes.

679
00:55:12,597 --> 00:55:16,943
Could I have food instead of milk?

680
00:55:17,131 --> 00:55:19,679
You were hungry?
I'll make you something right now.

681
00:55:19,704 --> 00:55:21,050
What do you want?

682
00:55:21,249 --> 00:55:23,043
Kimchi fried rice.

683
00:55:25,142 --> 00:55:28,564
You really are your mother's son, Gyeol.

684
00:55:37,689 --> 00:55:39,775
Heung Sik.

685
00:55:40,429 --> 00:55:42,542
Why did you agree to settle?

686
00:55:42,671 --> 00:55:44,857
I didn't do a single thing wrong.

687
00:55:45,376 --> 00:55:47,709
How did you not do anything wrong?

688
00:55:48,037 --> 00:55:51,633
You put a man in that state
and you did nothing wrong?

689
00:55:51,658 --> 00:55:53,171
That hurts!

690
00:55:53,672 --> 00:55:54,932
How much did you settle for?

691
00:55:54,957 --> 00:55:58,855
It cost me an arm and a leg. What now?

692
00:55:59,001 --> 00:56:02,556
That's it. Give me that wrist of yours.

693
00:56:02,611 --> 00:56:04,202
- So you can't cause more trouble,
- What is this, honestly.

694
00:56:04,236 --> 00:56:06,856
I'm starting with that wrist.

695
00:56:08,304 --> 00:56:10,094
Did you tell Gyu Rim?

696
00:56:10,548 --> 00:56:13,009
She can never find out about this.

697
00:56:13,457 --> 00:56:16,910
You think you're in any position...

698
00:56:17,010 --> 00:56:20,530
to worry about that family?

699
00:56:21,583 --> 00:56:23,208
Forget tenant protections.

700
00:56:23,248 --> 00:56:25,357
I'm throwing that family out right now.

701
00:56:25,377 --> 00:56:28,097
- Don't try to stop me.
- Just try throwing them out.

702
00:56:28,316 --> 00:56:30,484
That broken public restroom the other day,

703
00:56:30,509 --> 00:56:32,514
I'll put up a big poster...

704
00:56:32,539 --> 00:56:35,372
in the middle of the arcade saying
it was your doing.

705
00:56:35,397 --> 00:56:38,864
- Hey!
- Doesn't your conscience bother you?

706
00:56:38,889 --> 00:56:40,936
In good conscience, how can you pretend...

707
00:56:41,050 --> 00:56:42,363
What is it you want?

708
00:56:42,470 --> 00:56:44,957
The truth and an apology.

709
00:56:45,917 --> 00:56:49,150
The truth and an apology, my foot.

710
00:56:49,631 --> 00:56:54,284
To think
I gave birth to a snitch like you.

711
00:56:56,390 --> 00:56:59,137
I'll confess that it was me,

712
00:56:59,162 --> 00:57:01,622
and I'll pay the repair bill myself,

713
00:57:01,844 --> 00:57:05,003
so don't throw Gyu Rim's family out.

714
00:57:05,636 --> 00:57:10,076
Fine, burn it all down instead.

715
00:57:10,691 --> 00:57:15,001
They said tangling with a February Pig
would bring nothing but chaos,

716
00:57:15,026 --> 00:57:18,657
so fine. Burn it all down.

717
00:57:18,682 --> 00:57:20,350
What are you talking about?

718
00:57:20,375 --> 00:57:22,202
Who's a February Pig?

719
00:57:29,870 --> 00:57:33,170
All my friends warned me
to watch out for Cho Heung Sik.

720
00:57:33,370 --> 00:57:36,184
That he can't stand seeing others do well,

721
00:57:36,397 --> 00:57:41,509
that he's a notorious couple breaker,
and I should stay away from him.

722
00:57:41,857 --> 00:57:44,296
Am I insane? Was I drugged?

723
00:57:44,359 --> 00:57:46,557
With the woman I'm marrying
less than 3 meters away,

724
00:57:46,582 --> 00:57:49,351
why would I kiss a stranger?

725
00:57:52,383 --> 00:57:54,470
You can't chew apples, can you?

726
00:57:58,010 --> 00:58:01,431
You're all I have, Gyu Yeong. I mean it.

727
00:58:01,757 --> 00:58:03,670
What do I have to do
for you to believe me?

728
00:58:03,870 --> 00:58:06,404
Should I just die right here
in front of you?

729
00:58:07,111 --> 00:58:08,494
Why would you die?

730
00:58:08,519 --> 00:58:10,172
Just don't do it again.

731
00:58:11,183 --> 00:58:14,849
You don't believe me. You can't, can you?

732
00:58:16,237 --> 00:58:18,886
If that's all your heart amounts to,
forget it.

733
00:58:19,140 --> 00:58:21,172
Let's call the whole thing off.

734
00:58:22,355 --> 00:58:23,383
What is this?

735
00:58:26,670 --> 00:58:29,283
Has she lost her mind?

736
00:58:34,083 --> 00:58:35,456
Gyu Yeong.

737
00:58:35,691 --> 00:58:37,271
I'm not having a wedding.

738
00:58:43,017 --> 00:58:44,261
I was wrong.

739
00:58:44,382 --> 00:58:46,255
I was really wrong.

740
00:58:46,551 --> 00:58:49,744
I don't even remember this happening.

741
00:58:49,771 --> 00:58:52,791
The guys threw me a bachelor party
and got me so drunk...

742
00:58:52,792 --> 00:58:55,765
Let's skip the ceremony
and just take photos.

743
00:58:56,031 --> 00:58:58,064
In a wedding dress and a tuxedo.

744
00:58:58,089 --> 00:58:59,169
Sorry?

745
00:59:01,010 --> 00:59:04,810
So you'll marry me after all?

746
00:59:05,004 --> 00:59:09,544
And make a big show of telling guests
we donated the whole ceremony budget.

747
00:59:15,546 --> 00:59:18,971
Gyu Yeong, you really are...

748
00:59:19,164 --> 00:59:20,871
First thing tomorrow
at the district office,

749
00:59:20,909 --> 00:59:23,615
we're registering the marriage.
Just stamp it.

750
00:59:23,640 --> 00:59:25,373
I'll go by myself.

751
00:59:31,484 --> 00:59:35,383
Cheat whenever you want. Don't hold back.

752
00:59:36,451 --> 00:59:39,452
Then I can cheat right back
without a care.

753
00:59:39,477 --> 00:59:40,622
We're square, then?

754
00:59:41,664 --> 00:59:44,163
I always wondered how couples
who fake it for show live,

755
00:59:44,188 --> 00:59:45,667
so let's give it a try.

756
00:59:46,370 --> 00:59:48,223
Sounds like a blast, doesn't it?

757
01:00:16,943 --> 01:00:20,523
(Here Lies My Hope)

758
01:00:34,084 --> 01:00:37,271
It's Hye Jeong, Gyu Rim.

759
01:00:40,203 --> 01:00:42,298
No matter how hard I think about it,

760
01:00:42,607 --> 01:00:45,667
you're the only person I can turn to.

761
01:00:46,307 --> 01:00:51,029
Something came up and there's no way
I can raise this child.

762
01:00:51,490 --> 01:00:54,882
I'd be so grateful
if you raised him with yours,

763
01:00:55,203 --> 01:00:58,612
but if you can't, please
put him in an orphanage.

764
01:00:59,719 --> 01:01:02,479
I'm sorry. Please, Gyu Rim.

765
01:01:03,760 --> 01:01:07,773
(Baby Box)

766
01:01:58,863 --> 01:02:00,850
I'm leaving you behind.

767
01:02:03,617 --> 01:02:05,665
How can you not even cry?

768
01:02:10,010 --> 01:02:11,598
It breaks my heart.

769
01:02:25,430 --> 01:02:27,079
Is that right?

770
01:02:27,460 --> 01:02:29,047
All done.

771
01:02:29,956 --> 01:02:32,485
Han Gyeol, you can do it.

772
01:02:34,243 --> 01:02:35,648
You can roll over.

773
01:02:35,843 --> 01:02:37,735
Han Gyeol, come on.

774
01:02:38,088 --> 01:02:40,445
What? You rolled over?

775
01:02:40,842 --> 01:02:42,303
Lemon.

776
01:02:47,501 --> 01:02:48,686
Mama.

777
01:02:49,590 --> 01:02:50,997
Mama?

778
01:02:51,319 --> 01:02:54,115
Did you just say Mama?

779
01:03:01,000 --> 01:03:02,343
I'm your mom.

780
01:03:05,171 --> 01:03:07,204
I'm your mom, Gyeol.

781
01:03:13,204 --> 01:03:14,804
Where are you going?

782
01:03:40,310 --> 01:03:43,587
I heard Gyeol is over there?

783
01:03:45,050 --> 01:03:47,328
I was just about to call you.

784
01:03:51,343 --> 01:03:54,749
I'm sorry to keep troubling you.

785
01:03:54,937 --> 01:03:57,170
I'll get him washed up and put to bed.

786
01:03:59,190 --> 01:04:00,683
I'm sorry.

787
01:04:01,623 --> 01:04:03,257
I'm truly sorry.

788
01:04:04,509 --> 01:04:05,802
Have you been crying?

789
01:04:15,011 --> 01:04:16,064
No.

790
01:04:17,784 --> 01:04:18,997
Where are you right now?

791
01:04:22,050 --> 01:04:23,256
Where are you?

792
01:04:28,156 --> 01:04:29,429
I'm sorry.

793
01:04:29,534 --> 01:04:35,732
My brother will come get Gyeol
in the morning.

794
01:04:36,370 --> 01:04:38,341
If you could just send me the address...

795
01:04:38,478 --> 01:04:40,177
Where are you, Gyu Rim?

796
01:04:46,116 --> 01:04:47,809
I'm coming right now.

797
01:04:53,304 --> 01:04:56,236
I'm coming to you right now.
Where are you?

798
01:05:36,282 --> 01:05:38,722
(Love on the Menu)

799
01:05:38,747 --> 01:05:40,348
She loves you that much,

800
01:05:40,373 --> 01:05:42,005
so why do you keep hurting her?

801
01:05:42,030 --> 01:05:44,074
Strangely, I just keep getting angry.

802
01:05:44,099 --> 01:05:46,506
I went to the district office
and registered the marriage.

803
01:05:46,557 --> 01:05:48,567
We didn't agree to date. We're dating.

804
01:05:48,642 --> 01:05:49,912
Day one starts today.

805
01:05:49,937 --> 01:05:52,197
Let's stop playing games with people here.

806
01:05:52,222 --> 01:05:53,397
I don't care who it is.

807
01:05:53,422 --> 01:05:55,026
You know I like your mom, right?

808
01:05:55,051 --> 01:05:56,465
Since when?

809
01:05:56,490 --> 01:05:57,796
Since before you were born.

810
01:05:57,821 --> 01:06:00,521
I'm going to tell the truth.
But I'm scared.

811
01:06:00,550 --> 01:06:05,163
I can wait all night, so take your time.

812
01:06:06,071 --> 01:06:07,871
Dramaday.me
